this is supposed to return the list without its negative numbers (zero stays, order kept) but it misses some of them. python. fix it, keep the name drop_negatives, and have it return a new list and leave the input alone:

```python
def drop_negatives(nums):
    for x in nums:
        if x < 0:
            nums.remove(x)
    return nums
```

js. topThree(scores) should return the three highest numbers, highest first. fewer than three scores -> all of them, highest first; repeated scores each count; empty -> []. it should also leave the scores array as it was. it gives wrong answers as soon as a score is above 9 or below zero. fix it, same name:

```js
function topThree(scores) {
  return scores.sort().reverse().slice(0, 3);
}
```
